    [BugFix][Triton] Cast SwiGLU sigmoid input to FP32 (#19519)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Cast the `swiglu_quant` sigmoid input to FP32 to fix BF16 compilation
    failures with Triton Ascend 3.6.0, which rejects BF16 input to
    `tl.sigmoid`.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Restores the BF16 path with Triton Ascend 3.6.0. Intermediate
    computation uses FP32; output dtypes are unchanged.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Validated on **A2 (Ascend910B4-1)** and **A5 (Ascend950PR)** with formal
    triton-ascend **3.6.0**, Torch 2.10.0 and CANN 9.2.0. A2 used Python
    3.12.13; A5 used Python 3.11.10 with the existing vLLM 0.31.0 release
    environment.
    
    | Target | A2 | A5 |
    | --- | --- | --- |
    | `triton/test_swiglu_quant.py` | 8 passed | 8 passed |
    | `test_fused_moe.py::test_token_dispatcher_with_all_gather_quant` | 108
    passed | 108 passed |
    | **Total per device** | **116 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped** | **116
    passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped** |
    
    The original BF16 compilation failure was reproduced on both devices.
    All 108 MoE cases on each device entered the BF16 `swiglu_quant` path.
    Tests and assertions were unchanged; all patched pytest processes exited
    0.
    
    Existing isolated runtimes and native artifacts were reused. The A2
    environment retained NumPy/ONNX Runtime ABI and exit-time `ERR99999`
    logs. These were targeted tests, not full-directory, model-accuracy or
    performance validation.
    
    Results precede the subsequent comment-only removal; executable code is
    unchanged.
    
